{"kind":"artifact","text":"The public API surface an application outside this module imports to run on the gitseq kernel. Four acts and no projection: Init creates a sequence and binds it to the application for life, recording the binding as the log's first record so the signing key becomes the binding authority; Open verifies the sequence and only then hands it back to the application it is bound to, refusing anything else as verifiable but uninterpretable; Append signs one act with a caller's key and gives it a position; Records returns the verified ordered record stream. The outside application holds its own fold. No roster and no admission allowlist, because its actors are keys; kernel bounds and a bounded sequencer queue still apply. Proved by a second Go module built against this checkout that runs an application end to end, and by the negative half: that module cannot reach an internal package, and neither this package nor the host vocabulary under it depends on an application profile.","body":{"branch":"request/chess-item3-public-api","commit":"090f3416e33b91473ad3f425835d07ab213cec70","path":"host"}}